## 2️⃣ EVI TRAJECTORY

### What It Measures:
How emotional volatility (complexity/chaos) changed over time

### Method:
- Compares early tiers (Tier_4, Tier_5) vs recent tiers (Tier_1, Tier_2)
- Calculates: `mean(recent EVI) - mean(early EVI)`
- Uses tier-crossing logic to determine significance

### Thresholds (Statistically-Grounded):
```
+2 tiers crossed  → ↑↑ Rapidly Fragmenting
+1 tier crossed   → ↑ Fragmenting
0 tiers crossed   → → Stable Volatility
-1 tier crossed   → ↓ Consolidating
-2 tiers crossed  → ↓↓ Rapidly Consolidating
```

### What It Tells Us:

| Trend | What It Means | Example |
|---|---|---|
| ↑↑ Rapidly Fragmenting | Emotions becoming highly chaotic (2+ tier jump) | Stable (15) → High Volatility (65) |
| ↑ Fragmenting | Emotional complexity increasing | Low Vol (25) → Moderate Vol (45) |
| → Stable Volatility | Emotional consistency unchanged | Moderate Vol (50) → Moderate Vol (55) |
| ↓ Consolidating | Emotions converging into fewer states | High Vol (70) → Moderate Vol (50) |
| ↓↓ Rapidly Consolidating | Emotions hardening into single state (2+ tier drop) | Extreme Vol (85) → Low Vol (25) |

### Output Example:
```python
"EVI_trajectory": {
    "start": 22.1,           # Early tiers: Low Volatility
    "end": 72.4,             # Recent tiers: High Volatility
    "delta": +50.3,          # Massive increase
    "tier_shift": +2,        # Crossed 2 tiers upward
    "trend": "↑↑ Rapidly Fragmenting",
    "by_tier": {
        "Tier_1": 78.2,      # Extreme chaos now
        "Tier_2": 66.6,
        "Tier_3": 42.1,
        "Tier_4": 18.5,
        "Tier_5": 25.7       # Was stable
    }
}
```

### Autonomous Agent Uses This To:
- ✅ Detect relationship instability (fragmenting = unpredictable)
- ✅ Identify consolidation patterns:
  - Consolidating + Positive ERI = Maturing loyalty ✅
  - Consolidating + Negative ERI = Entrenching hatred ❌
- ✅ Flag chaos risks (fragmenting = intervention needed)

